b'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n     <head>\n          <title>Homepage</title> \n     </head>\n     <body>\n          <!--background image will rick roll you/text-align centers the text-->\n          <section style="background-image: url(https://i.imgur.com/OBB7tLg.gif); text-align: center; margin: auto; font-family: Comic Sans MS;">\n               <nav style="border: solid red 1px; background-color: red;"> \n                    <a href="/90.html">Home</a>\n                    <a href="pages/one-hit-wonders.html">One Hit Wonders</a>\n                    <a href="pages/top-90s-hits.html">Top 90s Hits</a>\n                    <a href="pages/90s-boy-bands.html">90s boy bands</a>\n               </nav>\n          <!-- div to help section stuff-->\n          <div style="width: calc(100% - 300px); margin: 10px auto; font-size: 8px;">\n               <!-- Main page header-->\n               <h1 style="font-size: 32px;">90s Music</h1>\n               <p>The 90s was the era of the good ol\' Britney Spears, girl groups, heartbreaking boy bands and some nice smellin\' teen spirit. On top of that, it was also the time of when techno and grunge become very popular. Some basic bands that most people think of, when it comes to the 90s, would probably be the:</p>\n               <!-- un ordered list of bands-->\n               <ul style="list-style-type: none; ">\n                    <li>Backstreet Boys</li>\n                    <li>Destiny\'s Child</li>\n                    <li>Nirvana</li>\n                    <li>Mc Hammer</li>\n                    <li>Spice Girls</li>\n               </ul> \n               <p>However, in reality there are a lot more bands and genres of music to the era. Find out below of some of the 90s music culture.</p>\n               <!--embeded youtube video-->\n               <embed width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/SgRXSLujJ5U">\n               <p style="font-size: 12px;">We have a video from our sponsors, who I don\'t really know of. There really is no sponsor either for this page. I guess wikipedia and Youtube could be it. ANYWAY, a video that they wanted to be included in this oh so wonderful 90s music page.</p>\n               <embed width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/fXpfdq3WYu4">\n               <marquee scrollamount="50"><img src="https://media.giphy.com/media/jM4bWFBKpSFeo/giphy.gif" style="transform: scaleX(-1);"></marquee>\n               <!-- video that scrolls across screen, but also loops and autoplays as soon as the page opens-->\n               <marquee scrollamount="70"><iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/dQw4w9WgXcQ?autoplay=1&loop=1" frameborder="0" width="50px" height="50px" loop></iframe></marquee>\n          </div>\n          <!-- Start of SimpleHitCounter Code -->\n          <div align="center">\n               <a href="http://www.simplehitcounter.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://simplehitcounter.com/hit.php?uid=0&f=16777215&b=0" border="0" height="18" width="83" alt="web counter"></a><br><a href="http://www.simplehitcounter.com" target="_blank" style="text-decoration:none;">web counter</a>\n          </div>\n          <!-- End of SimpleHitCounter Code -->\n\n          </section>\n     </body>\n</html>\n'

